.el .ds Aq '
.TH elfshaker-store 1  "store " 
.SH NAME
elfshaker\-store \- Stores the current state of the repository in a snapshot. The snapshots created in this way can later be packed in a .pack file using the pack command.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBelfshaker store\fR [\fB\-\-files\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-files0\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsnapshot\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Stores the current state of the repository in a snapshot. The snapshots created in this way can later be packed in a .pack file using the pack command.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-files\-from\fR \fI<file>\fR
Reads the list of files to include in the snapshot from the specified file. \*(Aq\-\*(Aq is taken to mean stdin.
.TP
\fB\-\-files0\-from\fR \fI<file>\fR
Reads the NUL\-separated (ASCII \\0) list of files to include in the snapshot from the specified file. \*(Aq\-\*(Aq is taken to mean stdin.
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enables verbose description of the execution process.
.TP
\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR [default: elfshaker_data]
Set the path to the elfshaker repository.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIsnapshot\fR>
The tag for the newly created snapshot.
